 Harry Potter in  the second movie installment Fantastic  Beasts the crimes of Grindelwald we  discovered that bikini not always been a  snake she was in fact at one time a  human Woman as a woman she was a  maledictus meaning she was born with a  blood curse that at first allowed her to  transform back and forth between a human  and a snake sadly as with all  maledictuses she eventually lost the  ability to control her Transformations  and the Affliction ultimately trapped  her in the form of a serpent this  beastial version of nagini was of course  the only one we used to know the  unusually intelligent and malevolent pet  Serpent of Lord Voldemort but with the  telling of the Guinea's origin story we  are shown the type of woman she was  before she became Voldemort's loyal pets  and it wouldn't be shocked if many of  you like myself were quite surprised to  find that the guinea was not completely  terrible as a human in fact it would  seem that she was actually quite moral  and good let me explain in Fantastic  Beasts the crimes of Grindelwald we are  introduced to nagini through Credence a  wayward Wizard and obscurial who was in  search of Clues to his past greentz  meets nagini after he joins a traveling  Wizarding Circus the circus arcanus and  the two form a close friendship we  witness nagini be kind and compassionate  towards Credence and she becomes  concerned when he shows interest in  joining the powerful dark wizard Gellert  Grindelwald ultimately despite caring  for Credence the guinea chooses to help  the likes of newt's commander and Albus  Dumbledore in their efforts to defeat  Grindelwald a far cry from where she  ends up with the Wizarding world's next  Great Dark Lord Voldemort which brings  us to the question if nagini was once a  good and kind woman how and when did she  turn so evil was it in fact when  Voldemort turned her into his horcrux in  all honesty I rather think not here's  why if being made into a horcrux had the  ability to turn the vessel of the  horcrux into an evil creature or being  wouldn't Harry Potter become undeniably  evil himself when Voldemort  unintentionally turned him into one as a  baby yes right but of course course we  know that didn't happen even if Harry  wasn't a full-on horcrux in fact we  didn't even know that Harry was a  horcrux until the very end of the final  installment of the series it was a good  wizard he was a moral person who is  maybe a little stubborn and misguided at  times but evil Harry never so then why  did nagini turn so evil if not from  being made into the Dark Lord's Hawk  racks I think the answer to that is not  a simple one as a maledictus at first  nagini had the ability to go back and  forth between her two forms that if a  woman that of a snake I wouldn't be  surprised if she had found it quite  fascinating to start with she may have  even enjoyed it at one time or another  but once she permanently became a snake  can you imagine how trapped and isolated  she would have felt knowing that she  would never be able to interact with the  world as a human ever again she had no  one to talk to no one to pass a time  with to be perfectly honest it would be  enough to make anyone go mad really  don't you think but then again bad  redness does not necessarily equate to  being evil Q Lord Voldemort okay so how  exactly did nagini and Voldemort meet  her a maladictus serpent and he a  phantom-like version of himself due to  his failed attempt to murder an  infantary well the theory goes that deep  in the forest of Albania nagini met the  shadowy remains of the dark lord it was  here that he was rumored to have  befriended many of the animals that he  came across in the woods which of course  included nagini and so finally she had  found someone or something with whom she  could communicate Voldemort who could  speak to her in parcel tongue was also  able to inhabit her body it's not that  far-fetched to think that an  impenetrable Bond would have formed  especially on nagini's behalf and so  nagini having been driven a little bit  mad due to her isolation from humanity  and living in the woods as a beast  likely would have been all too open to  well whatever her new best mate  Voldemort suggested especially if it  included her sticking with him when he  left the forest of Albania this would  have been a very unique maybe even once  in a lifetime opportunity for nagini an  opportunity for her to rejoin the  Wizarding World in a way she probably  hadn't thought possible before meeting  Voldemort after all parcel tongue was an  incredibly rare language and yet it was  this wizard who could understand and  talk to her I can only imagine this  would have come as an intense relief for  nikini from there well we know the rest  nagini became Voldemort's most loyal pet  it was nagini who helped him regain his  strength while in his shadow form her  Venom was a key part of the potion that  enabled him to return to a temporary  body and then nagini herself was made  into a horcrux further helping him  return to power when Voldemort took the  life of Bertha jawkins after that they  were rarely separated she witnessed him  before murder after murder and she  killed on his behalf and was constantly  all of this clearly shows that nagini  most certainly did turn evil but I  believe she did so long before becoming  one of Voldemort's horcruxes and so in  my opinion Nikki still would have become  evil even if she hadn't been made into a  horcrux she may have even turned evil  without having met this particular dark  lord after all maledictus has lost the  ability to think like a human as time  went on so it's possible that she may  have become more and more wicked as she  lived life permanently as a snake  but since it's not inevitable for  maledictus to become evil despite the  Affliction coming from a blood curse I  think that the main reason nagini turned  evil was her relationship with Voldemort  rather than any form of magic but curse  horcrux or otherwise in her desperation  to connect with the being more  intelligent than the Woodland creatures  she lived amongst in the forest of  Albania she was willing to be whatever  the dark lord needed her to be and that  just so happened to be an evil serpent  willing to do his bidding  which brings us to the end of this video  what do you guys think do you agree that  it was nagini's relationship with  Voldemort that turned her evil or do you  think she was already poised and ready  to be evil on her own when he met her or  was it something else entirely let me  know your thoughts in the comments below  and don't forget to like the video and  subscribe to the channel until next time  dinner nagini  [Music]

